      "body": "> Hi thank you for your interests in our work!\n> \n> Squidiff is not a foundation model so the checkpoints only work for a limited set of related datasets, if you have your own datasets, it's better to pretrain it without many GPUs.\n> \n> We will also release our checkpoints for the study we discussed in the paper in the following days.\n\nHi Siyu,\n\nI see~ \n\nThanks for the swift reply, we're currently preparing a new large scale drug perturbation dataset (somewhat similar to LINCS), this would be beneficial for evaluating the OOD ability of other models that specifically developed for drug perturbations, and we are trying to build our own prediction model based on these data. \n\nCongratulation again and looking forward to your future work or potential collaborations.",
